8.	Write a command to display system uptime and logged-in users together.
Command:
uptime && who
Explanation:
•	uptime → shows how long the system has been running, number of users, and load averages.
•	&& → runs the next command only if the previous command succeeds.
•	who → lists all currently logged-in users.
✅ Example output:
 19:35:01 up  3:42,  2 users,  load average: 0.15, 0.10, 0.08
